WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.158
A terrible day. Is there nothing else to write?

00:00:03.158 --> 00:00:06.316
Keep the difficulty. Notice the support too.

00:00:06.316 --> 00:00:09.474
A 2003 study compared different journaling activities.

00:00:09.474 --> 00:00:12.632
Conditions focused on blessings, hassles or everyday events.

00:00:12.632 --> 00:00:15.789
Several affect and well-being outcomes were examined.

00:00:15.789 --> 00:00:22.105
First record what actually happened.

00:00:22.105 --> 00:00:28.421
Notice one specific thing that helped.

00:00:28.421 --> 00:00:34.737
It might be an umbrella or quiet company.

00:00:34.737 --> 00:00:41.053
Difficulty and support can share one page.

00:00:41.053 --> 00:00:44.211
Some group benefits do not guarantee individual benefits.

00:00:44.211 --> 00:00:47.368
You need not thank someone for harming you.

00:00:47.368 --> 00:00:50.526
Gratitude journaling does not replace treatment.

00:00:50.526 --> 00:00:56.842
If you wish, record who helped, how and when.

00:00:56.842 --> 00:01:03.158
Keep the unresolved problems in the account.

00:01:03.158 --> 00:01:06.316
Adjust or stop if it feels burdensome or unhelpful.

00:01:06.316 --> 00:01:09.474
The day can remain hard without pretending otherwise.

00:01:09.474 --> 00:01:12.632
The umbrella was real as well.

00:01:12.632 --> 00:01:15.789
Thank you for being there.
